{%- comment -%}
  Outputs "true" when a piece of product media is an illustration rather
  than product photography, and so belongs in a storytelling section rather
  than the gallery.

  Accepts:
  - media: {Object} a product media object
  - keys: {String} comma-separated fragments, from the template's
    "Illustration filenames" setting

  Matching is on the file name. Shopify gives these uploads no alt text to
  match on, and media has no tag or type of its own that separates a drawing
  from a photograph. With no keys nothing matches, which is why every other
  template keeps all of its media in the gallery.

  Only the base name is matched, never the whole URL. image_url returns an
  absolute address on the shop's own domain, so matching the URL would test
  the keys against "ohbettyjaletti.com" as well and a key like "betty" would
  quietly swallow every photograph on the page.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign is_illustration = false

  if keys != blank and media != blank
    assign needles = keys | downcase | split: ','
    assign media_src = media.preview_image | image_url: width: 1 | split: '?' | first | split: '/' | last | downcase

    for needle in needles
      assign fragment = needle | strip
      if fragment != blank and media_src contains fragment
        assign is_illustration = true
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}
{%- if is_illustration -%}true{%- endif -%}
